How about improving the Amulet's portal detection so you don't have to
stumble all around the Plane hoping it'll feel warm while you're near
the portal.

Once you're at "feels very warm" you're close enough for a secret door
detection effect to find the portal; that's probably not a "trick",
although it might not be entirely obvious.  However, getting within
that distance is tricky, especially with only 1/15 game turns giving a
message (and you're probably [very] fast).

I'm not sure if simply increasing the message frequency would be
sufficient...maybe a compass effect instead of/in addition to the warm
feeling.  "You feel the Amulet of Yendor pulling to the northeast."

I wonder how a 1/10 compass direction when worn/wielded would do for
triangulation.  Would probably get you close enough to either sdd or
just stumble into the portal pretty reasonably.


